# Periodic jobs run by the scheduler service (supercronic, see docker-compose.yml).
#
# Format: standard 5-field cron + command.
#   minute  hour  day-of-month  month  day-of-week  command
# All times are UTC (the container's clock).
#
# Each command invokes a Python module that wraps its body in
# `fx_pulse.jobs.track_run`, so every run is recorded in the `job_runs`
# table and surfaced on the Grafana dashboard.
#
# To add a job:
#   1. Write fx_pulse/<job_name>.py using `with track_run(conn, "<job_name>"):`.
#   2. Add one cron line below.
#   3. Add a `make <job_name>` target for manual triggers.
#
# Daily catch-up backfill for yesterday's UTC window at S5 (5-second)
# candles. With no `--date`, fill_day defaults to yesterday UTC.
# Idempotent against the live streamer via tick_id ON CONFLICT, so safe
# even when the streamer covered the same window.
30 1 * * * uv run python -m fx_pulse.fill_day

# RBA cash-rate-target ingest — 02:05 UTC on the 5th of each month.
# RBA refreshes the source daily, but cash-rate-target rows only change
# ~8x/year on decision dates; monthly cadence is plenty and keeps
# job_runs uncluttered.
5 2 5 * * uv run python -m fx_pulse.ingest.rba_cash_rate
